# Node documentation

- These Markdown files are user-facing node help, embedded by the catalog.
  Keep Chinese and English versions equivalent and register both in the existing
  documentation mapping. Short catalog descriptions are not a substitute.
- Describe the actual node input, parameter defaults/ranges, preprocessing,
  output fields and limitations after checking Catalog, Kernel, Runtime and SCI.
- For each implemented test or selectable variant, state its purpose, null and
  alternative hypotheses, statistic formula, symbol definitions, reference
  distribution, degrees of freedom and p-value/rejection rule separately.
- Expand named intermediate quantities needed to reproduce the calculation.
  Specify moment denominators, kurtosis convention, weighting and lag/horizon
  indexing when relevant. Do not replace a formula with only a method name.
- Explain sample-size and model assumptions, degenerate inputs and what a
  non-significant result does and does not establish. Descriptive diagnostics,
  response functions and decompositions must not invent tests or p-values.
- Include a practical interpretation/example and authoritative references for
  statistical methods. Distinguish implementation conventions from general theory.
- Use `$...$` and `$$...$$` math supported by the existing Markdown renderer;
  verify changed formulas render. Keep maintenance rules and backend paths out
  of user-facing prose.
